i         U+0131 LATIN SMALL LETTER DOTLESS I            no   no
i         U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE   no   no
i U+0307  U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE   no   no

does /i fold the BACKREFERENCE comparison too?
(a)\1 /i     vs 'a' + U+0041            yes
(k)\1 /iu    vs 'k' + U+212A            yes

one program, two answers about the same pair
  toUpperCase(U+00DF) === 'SS'      true    regex /iu:  no
  toLowerCase(U+212A) === 'k'       true    regex /iu:  yes
